  "body": "**What happens now.** A Wire Contour lead goes in a straight line from the start hole to the nearest point of the wire path. On a circle, this lead is radial. The wire stops and turns at the entry point. This can leave a small dwell mark on the part.\n\n**What we want.** An option next to the straight lead: a short tangent arc lead-in and lead-out. The lead goes from the start hole to the start of a short arc. The arc meets the contour tangentially at the entry point. The lead-out is the mirror of the lead-in. The wire then enters and leaves without a stop at the contour.\n\n**Rules.**\n- The straight lead stays the default. The arc lead is opt-in. The existing goldens do not change.\n- The arc radius has a stated rule (a user value with a default, limited by the hole distance and by the kerf).\n- When no tangent arc lead fits, the operation refuses by name. It does not clamp the radius silently, and it does not go back to the straight lead silently.\n- The existing wire laws (the lead stays in the waste and clears the product by the kerf) and the simulation verifier check the arc lead.\n- Posts: generic ISO, Sodick and G-EDM write the lead arc as G02/G03. Sodick keeps its rule that the first move is straight: the move from the hole to the arc start is that straight move.\n- The option has an MCP field, a project-file field (serde default; old projects do not change) and a UI row.\n\n**Done means.**\n- A die circle and a line+arc punch cut with the arc lead. The lead is tangent at the entry. The laws are clean.\n- A hole that is too near and an arc that crosses the profile are refused by name.\n- New post goldens for ISO, Sodick and G-EDM with the arc lead. The straight-lead goldens do not change.\n- The MCP field and the project file round-trip the option.\n\nSuggested labels (I cannot set labels): `P6`, `effort:high`, `area:2d`, `source:agent`.\n\nRefs #3937\n",
